  { question: "How do I file a no-fault insurance claim in Wayne County?", answer: "Notify your insurance company as soon as possible after the accident—ideally within 24 to 48 hours. Most policies require written notice within 30 days. Complete the application for benefits your insurer provides, and submit supporting documentation including medical records, wage documentation, and receipts for replacement services. If your insurance company denies benefits or fails to pay promptly, you have the right to file a lawsuit. Our attorneys guide you through every step and protect your rights throughout the process." },
